      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the structure. Let me write the improved test file with better understandability: formatted data providers, explanatory comments for the magic byte values, a named constant for the specifier, and removal of unused data-provider methods.Now I'll compile-check it.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file adds a named constant `ARBITRARY_CODEC_SPECIFIER = 116` to replace the magic number, reformats the data provider to one entry per line with inline comments decoding each byte sequence into its BHSD parameters, adds a class-level Javadoc explaining the encoding scheme, and removes the four unused data-provider methods that cluttered the original file."
